+      is requested: the plans are the branch's own bookkeeping and add no design the first
+      category does not already carry.
+
+  - name: stm-run-records
+    playbook: null
+    playbook_missing: true
+    design_bearing: false   # machine-written run artifacts and play outputs; no design content
+    evidence:
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/analysis.yaml          # analyze-changes output (commit grouping)
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/branch.json            # context receipt
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/commits.yaml           # commit-change record (commits and their files)
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/issue.json             # context receipt
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/plan-check.json        # plan checker receipt (valid, now 4)
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/porcelain.txt          # git status snapshot from an earlier moment
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/pr-body.md             # propose-change output (PR body)
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/pr.json                # context receipt (PR #666)
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/resolved-rules.json    # context receipt (self-review rule path)
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/self-review.md         # propose-change output (informational self-review)
+      - .garura/project/issues/655/context/work-description.txt   # work description
+    notes: >
+      Same category as in the #665 review (654): play run records (receipts, snapshots, JSON
+      context, the self-review and PR body). No playbook covers it. Suggested treatment: skim
+      only for consistency. self-review.md is a point-in-time record of an earlier state of the
+      branch (it counts 14 samples, 6 broken samples, 33 files and a 486-line contract; the
+      final branch has 15, 12 and 45, and the fix commit 0066c32e followed it), while pr-body.md
+      is current (15 samples, 12 broken, 20 tests); the PR body's "Fixed before raising" list is
+      what bridges the two. No design-grounding.
+design_bearing_categories:
+  - tool-interface-contract   # new category, no playbook; the fan-out runs one grounding dispatch for it (width one)
+absent_seeded_categories: [decision-records, harness, memory, config-maps]
+path_accounting:   # 28 + 1 + 1 + 1 + 3 + 11 = 45
