+      the only route is reject and propose again, and adding it later is a new contract
+      version. (2) The approval is not tied to the words approved: ADR 033's pattern is "a
+      person accepted these exact words" with a fingerprint, who and when; here the update
+      keeps who, when and the reply but no fingerprint of the draft the person saw, so an
+      engine that lets a draft change between propose and decide cannot be caught by the
+      contract.
+    principle_violated: ADR033-APPROVAL-IS-ABOUT-EXACT-WORDS
+    committed_source: "docs/adr/033 Decision part 2; .garura/project/issues/653/specs/plan.md item 11 (main)"
+    suggested_direction: >
+      Add `draft_fingerprint` to decide (and keep it on the update), and either add a change
+      verdict now or record in plan item 11 that a v2 adds it.
+  - id: TIC-12
+    severity: P3
+    file: "core/tools/memory/contract/v1.json (description line 6); core/tools/memory/README.md (line 41 'On the command line its fields are the flags')"
+    finding: >
+      ADR 035 part 4 and the KB note make the agent-facing surface a command-line tool, and
+      the plan has the contract say "what each returns". The command-line form is defined by one
+      sentence ("its fields are the flags"). cite and propose carry an array of objects
+      (`sources`), which has no flag form; nothing says how a boolean, an array or a multi-line
+      draft is passed, what stdout and stderr carry, or what the exit code is for ok:false. #657
+      builds the tool and #661 and #663 write agent calls against it, so each will have to
+      invent this.
+    principle_violated: ADR035-S4-ONE-TOOL
+    committed_source: "docs/adr/035 Decision part 4; core/components/memory/knowledge/_DESIGN.md 'Final' (a CLI) (main)"
+    suggested_direction: >
+      Add a short CLI mapping to the contract: a command name, flags for scalar fields, a
+      `--json` or stdin form for any request, JSON on stdout for every answer, and an exit code
+      rule. One sample per form.
+  - id: TIC-13
+    severity: P4
+    file: "core/tools/memory/contract/v1.json (version '1.0.0', contract_version '1', cite summary line 311); core/tools/memory/README.md ('The contract changes only by a new version')"
+    finding: >
+      Two version fields in one file (naming clarity) and a rule that every change is a new
+      version, while the contract itself says the cite shape will be refined by the citations
+      story. Each refinement, and TIC-3, TIC-11 and TIC-12 if taken later, then forces v2 and a
+      rewrite of the const "1" in every response. No committed source defines the rule, so this
+      is an observation.
+    principle_violated: null
+    committed_source: null
+    suggested_direction: >
+      State what counts as additive (an optional field) and stays version 1, and which of the two
+      version fields a caller reads.
+  - id: TIC-14
+    severity: P4
+    file: "core/tools/memory/contract/v1.json ($defs.draft_source lines 821-828, $defs.source); core/tools/memory/contract/samples/broken/propose-unknown-draft-source.json"
+    finding: >
+      Plan item 5 asks that the draft's origin is marked (person, web, model). The contract
+      marks it, and adds a fourth value, memory, that no committed source names. A web or model
+      draft carries only the category: `sources` can name memory pieces only, and `sources: []`
+      is accepted for a web draft (verification vi), so the person approving cannot see which
+      page the draft came from unless it is in the free text.
+    principle_violated: null
+    committed_source: ".garura/project/issues/653/specs/plan.md item 5 (main)"
+    suggested_direction: >
+      Add an optional `origin` string (a URL or a name) required when draft_source is web, and
+      note why memory was added.
+
+status: completed
+notes: >
+  Counts: P1 0, P2 3, P3 9, P4 2 (14 findings). Every principle is cited to a file on main or to
+  a read-only issue text; nothing was grounded in v1.json, the README, the new 655 plan or the PR
+  body. Where a committed source was only partly applicable it is said so (ADR 033 is about the
+  product model and is used as the pattern ADR 035 lists as Related; the glossary's Memory
+  Architecture section predates ADR 035 and was used only for the STM definition ADR 035 keeps).
+  The most important single point is TIC-1 together with TIC-2: the contract carries the
+  approval flow as words, and the check does not test it. A missing playbook for this kind of
+  work (a tool's interface contract) stands: categories.yaml lists it under missing_playbooks.
+  The Layer-2 dispatch cannot create tasks (no TaskCreate tool in this agent's tool set), so the
+  follow-up task for the missing playbook is left to the play.
